msgstr "Problema estimării fazei {#the-phase-estimation-problem}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This section of the lesson explains the *phase estimation problem*.\n"
"We'll begin with a short discussion of the *spectral theorem* from linear algebra, and then move on to a statement of the phase estimation problem itself.\n"
msgstr ""
"Această secțiune a lecției explică *problema estimării fazei*.\n"
"Vom începe cu o scurtă discuție despre *teorema spectrală* din algebră liniară, apoi vom trece la enunțarea problemei estimării fazei în sine.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spectral theorem {#spectral-theorem}"
msgstr "Teorema spectrală {#spectral-theorem}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The *spectral theorem* is an important fact from linear algebra that states that matrices of a certain type, called *normal matrices,* can be expressed in a simple and useful way.\n"
"We'll only need this theorem for unitary matrices in this lesson, but down the road in this series we'll apply it to Hermitian matrices as well.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Teorema spectrală* este un rezultat important din algebră liniară care afirmă că matricele de un anumit tip, numite *matrice normale,* pot fi exprimate într-un mod simplu și util.\n"
"Vom avea nevoie de această teoremă doar pentru matrice unitare în această lecție, dar mai departe în această serie o vom aplica și matricelor hermitice.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Normal matrices {#normal-matrices}"
msgstr "Matrice normale {#normal-matrices}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A square matrix $M$ with complex number entries is said to be a *normal* matrix if it commutes with its conjugate transpose:\n"
"$M M^{\\dagger} = M^{\\dagger} M$.\n"
msgstr ""
"O matrice pătrată $M$ cu intrări numere complexe se numește matrice *normală* dacă comută cu transpusa sa conjugată:\n"
"$M M^{\\dagger} = M^{\\dagger} M.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every unitary matrix $U$ is normal because\n"
msgstr "Orice matrice unitară $U$ este normală deoarece\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U U^{\\dagger} = \\mathbb{I} = U^{\\dagger} U.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U U^{\\dagger} = \\mathbb{I} = U^{\\dagger} U.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Hermitian matrices, which are matrices that equal their own conjugate transpose, are another important class of normal matrices.\n"
"If $H$ is a Hermitian matrix, then\n"
msgstr ""
"Matricele hermitice, care sunt matrice egale cu propria lor transpusă conjugată, reprezintă o altă clasă importantă de matrice normale.\n"
"Dacă $H$ este o matrice hermitică, atunci\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H H^{\\dagger} = H^2 = H^{\\dagger} H,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H H^{\\dagger} = H^2 = H^{\\dagger} H,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "so $H$ is normal.\n"
msgstr "deci $H$ este normală.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Not every square matrix is normal.\n"
"For instance, this matrix isn't normal:\n"
msgstr ""
"Nu orice matrice pătrată este normală.\n"
"De exemplu, această matrice nu este normală:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(This is a simple but great example of a matrix that's often very helpful to consider.)\n"
"It isn't normal because\n"
msgstr ""
"(Acesta este un exemplu simplu, dar excelent de matrice care este adesea foarte util de luat în considerare.)\n"
"Nu este normală deoarece\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^{\\dagger}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^{\\dagger}\n"
"=\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "while\n"
msgstr "în timp ce\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^{\\dagger}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}^{\\dagger}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\\\\\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Theorem statement {#theorem-statement}"
msgstr "Enunțul teoremei {#theorem-statement}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now here's a statement of the spectral theorem.\n"
msgstr "Iată acum un enunț al teoremei spectrale.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Theorem\">\n"
"Spectral theorem: Let $M$ be a normal $N\\times N$ complex matrix.\n"
"There exists an orthonormal basis of $N$-dimensional complex vectors $\\bigl\\{ \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_N\\rangle \\bigr\\}$ along with complex numbers $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N$ such that\n"
"$$\n"
"M = \\lambda_1 \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_1\\vert + \\cdots + \\lambda_N \\vert \\psi_N\\rangle\\langle \\psi_N\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Teoremă\">\n"
"Teorema spectrală: Fie $M$ o matrice complexă normală de dimensiune $N\\times N$.\n"
"Există o bază ortonormată de vectori complexi $N$-dimensionali $\\bigl\\{ \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_N\\rangle \\bigr\\}$ împreună cu numerele complexe $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N$ astfel încât\n"
"$$\n"
"M = \\lambda_1 \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_1\\vert + \\cdots + \\lambda_N \\vert \\psi_N\\rangle\\langle \\psi_N\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
"</Figure>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The expression of a matrix in the form\n"
msgstr "Expresia unei matrice în forma\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert \\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert \\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is commonly called a *spectral decomposition*.\n"
"Notice that if $M$ is a normal matrix expressed in the form $(1)$, then the equation\n"
msgstr ""
"se numește în mod obișnuit *descompunere spectrală*.\n"
"Observă că dacă $M$ este o matrice normală exprimată în forma $(1)$, atunci ecuația\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle = \\lambda_j \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle = \\lambda_j \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"must be true for every $j = 1,\\ldots,N$.\n"
"This is a consequence of the fact that $\\bigl\\{ \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_N\\rangle \\bigr\\}$ is orthonormal:\n"
msgstr ""
"trebuie să fie adevărată pentru orice $j = 1,\\ldots,N$.\n"
"Aceasta este o consecință a faptului că $\\bigl\\{ \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_N\\rangle \\bigr\\}$ este ortonormată:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"= \\left(\\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\right)\\vert \\psi_j\\rangle\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"= \\lambda_j \\vert\\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"= \\left(\\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\right)\\vert \\psi_j\\rangle\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 1}^N \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"= \\lambda_j \\vert\\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That is, each number $\\lambda_j$ is an *eigenvalue* of $M$ and $\\vert\\psi_j\\rangle$ is an *eigenvector* corresponding to that eigenvalue.\n"
msgstr "Cu alte cuvinte, fiecare număr $\\lambda_j$ este o *valoare proprie* a lui $M$, iar $\\vert\\psi_j\\rangle$ este un *vector propriu* corespunzător acelei valori proprii.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Example 1**.\n"
"Let\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{I} = \\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0\\\\0 & 1\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"**Exemplul 1**.\n"
"Fie\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{I} = \\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0\\\\0 & 1\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  which is normal.\n"
"  The theorem implies that $\\mathbb{I}$ can be written in the form $(1)$ for some choice of $\\lambda_1$, $\\lambda_2$, $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle$, and $\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle$.\n"
"  There are multiple choices that work, including\n"
msgstr ""
"  care este normală.\n"
"  Teorema implică faptul că $\\mathbb{I}$ poate fi scrisă în forma $(1)$ pentru o anumită alegere a lui $\\lambda_1,$ $\\lambda_2,$ $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,$ și $\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle.$\n"
"  Există mai multe alegeri care funcționează, inclusiv\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\lambda_1 = 1, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\lambda_2 = 1, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle = \\vert 0\\rangle, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_2\\rangle = \\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\lambda_1 = 1, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\lambda_2 = 1, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle = \\vert 0\\rangle, \\hspace{5pt}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_2\\rangle = \\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Notice that the theorem does not say that the complex numbers $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N$ are\n"
"  distinct — we can have the same complex number repeated, which is necessary for this example.\n"
"  These choices work because\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\mathbb{I} = \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  Observă că teorema nu afirmă că numerele complexe $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N$ sunt\n"
"  distincte — același număr complex poate apărea repetat, ceea ce este necesar în acest exemplu.\n"
"  Aceste alegeri funcționează deoarece\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\mathbb{I} = \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert.\n"
"  $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Indeed, we could choose $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle\\}$ to be *any* orthonormal basis and the\n"
"  equation will be true. For instance,\n"
msgstr ""
"  Într-adevăr, am putea alege $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle\\}$ să fie *orice* bază ortonormată și\n"
"  ecuația va fi adevărată. De exemplu,\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\mathbb{I} = \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert + \\vert -\\rangle\\langle -\\vert.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\mathbb{I} = \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert + \\vert -\\rangle\\langle -\\vert.\n"
"  $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Example 2**.\n"
"Consider a Hadamard operation.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Exemplul 2**.\n"
"Consideră o operație Hadamard.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  H = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  1 & 1\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  1 & -1\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  H = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  1 & 1\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  1 & -1\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  This is a unitary matrix, so it is normal. The spectral theorem implies that $H$ can be written in the\n"
"  form $(1)$, and in particular we have\n"
msgstr ""
"  Aceasta este o matrice unitară, deci este normală. Teorema spectrală implică faptul că $H$ poate fi scrisă în\n"
"  forma $(1)$, și în particular avem\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  H =\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  - \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  H =\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  - \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  where\n"
msgstr "  unde\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle\n"
"  = \\cos(\\theta)\\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle\n"
"  = \\cos(\\theta)\\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  $$\n"
"  Mai explicit,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  More explicitly,\n"
msgstr "  Mai explicit,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle, \\\\[3mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle & = -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  \\end{aligned}\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle, \\\\[3mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle & = -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"  + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle.\n"
"  \\end{aligned}\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  We can check that this decomposition is correct by performing the required calculations:\n"
msgstr "  Putem verifica dacă această descompunere este corectă efectuând calculele necesare:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  - \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  -\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  = H.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  - \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle \\langle \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert\n"
"  = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  -\n"
"  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"  \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"  = H.\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As the first example above reveals, there can be some freedom in how eigenvectors are selected.\n"
"There is, however, no freedom at all in how the eigenvalues are chosen, except for their ordering:\n"
"the same $N$ complex numbers $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N$, which can include repetitions of the same complex number, will always occur in the equation $(1)$ for a given choice of a matrix $M$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Așa cum dezvăluie primul exemplu de mai sus, poate exista o anumită libertate în modul în care sunt selectați vectorii proprii.\n"
"Nu există, totuși, nicio libertate în modul în care sunt alese valorile proprii, cu excepția ordinii lor:\n"
"aceleași $N$ numere complexe $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_N$, care pot include repetiții ale aceluiași număr complex, vor apărea întotdeauna în ecuația $(1)$ pentru o alegere dată a unei matrice $M$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's focus in on unitary matrices.\n"
"Suppose we have a complex number $\\lambda$ and a non-zero vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ that satisfy the equation\n"
msgstr ""
"Acum să ne concentrăm pe matricele unitare.\n"
"Să presupunem că avem un număr complex $\\lambda$ și un vector nenul $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ care satisfac ecuația\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\lambda\\vert\\psi\\rangle.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\lambda\\vert\\psi\\rangle.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That is, $\\lambda$ is an eigenvalue of $U$ and $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is an eigenvector corresponding to this eigenvalue.\n"
msgstr "Adică, $\\lambda$ este o valoare proprie a lui $U$, iar $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ este un vector propriu corespunzător acestei valori proprii.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unitary matrices preserve Euclidean norm, and so we conclude the following from $(2)$.\n"
msgstr "Matricele unitare păstrează norma euclidiană, și astfel concluzionăm următoarele din $(2)$.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\bigl\\| U \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\bigl\\| \\lambda \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\vert \\lambda \\vert \\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\bigl\\| U \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\bigl\\| \\lambda \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"= \\vert \\lambda \\vert \\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The condition that $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is non-zero implies that $\\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\\neq 0$, so we can cancel it from both sides to obtain\n"
msgstr "Condiția ca $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ să fie nenul implică faptul că $\\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|\\neq 0$, deci putem să o eliminăm din ambele părți pentru a obține\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\lambda \\vert = 1.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\lambda \\vert = 1.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This reveals that eigenvalues of unitary matrices must always have absolute value equal to one, so they lie on the *unit circle.*\n"
msgstr "Acest lucru dezvăluie că valorile proprii ale matricelor unitare trebuie să aibă întotdeauna valoarea absolută egală cu unu, deci se află pe *cercul unitate.*\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{T} = \\{\\alpha\\in\\mathbb{C} : \\vert\\alpha\\vert = 1\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{T} = \\{\\alpha\\in\\mathbb{C} : \\vert\\alpha\\vert = 1\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(The symbol $\\mathbb{T}$ is a common name for the complex unit circle. The name $S^1$ is also common.)\n"
msgstr "(Simbolul $\\mathbb{T}$ este un nume comun pentru cercul unitate complex. Numele $S^1$ este de asemenea comun.)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Phase estimation problem statement {#phase-estimation-problem-statement}"
msgstr "Enunțul problemei de estimare a fazei {#phase-estimation-problem-statement}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the *phase estimation problem*, we're given a quantum state $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ of $n$ qubits, along with a unitary quantum circuit that acts on $n$ qubits.\n"
"We're *promised* that $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ is an eigenvector of the unitary matrix $U$ that describes the action of the circuit, and our goal is to compute or approximate the eigenvalue $\\lambda$ to which $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ corresponds.\n"
"More precisely, because $\\lambda$ lies on the complex unit circle, we can write\n"
msgstr ""
"În *problema estimării fazei*, ni se dă o stare cuantică $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ pe $n$ qubiți, împreună cu un circuit cuantic unitar care acționează pe $n$ qubiți.\n"
"Se *garantează* că $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ este un vector propriu al matricei unitare $U$ care descrie acțiunea circuitului, iar scopul nostru este să calculăm sau să aproximăm valoarea proprie $\\lambda$ căreia îi corespunde $\\vert \\psi\\rangle.$\n"
"Mai precis, deoarece $\\lambda$ se află pe cercul unitate complex, putem scrie\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\lambda = e^{2\\pi i \\theta}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\lambda = e^{2\\pi i \\theta}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for a unique real number $\\theta$ satisfying $0\\leq\\theta<1$.\n"
"The goal of the problem is to compute or approximate this real number $\\theta$.\n"
msgstr ""
"pentru un număr real unic $\\theta$ care satisface $0\\leq\\theta<1$.\n"
"Scopul problemei este să calculăm sau să aproximăm acest număr real $\\theta$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Phase estimation problem\">\n"
"Input: A unitary quantum circuit for an $n$-qubit operation $U$ along with an $n$-qubit quantum state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ \\\n"
"Promise: $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is an eigenvector of $U$ \\\n"
"Output: an approximation to the number $\\theta\\in[0,1)$ satisfying $U\\vert\\psi\\rangle = e^{2\\pi i \\theta}\\vert\\psi\\rangle$\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Problema estimării fazei\">\n"
"Intrare: Un circuit cuantic unitar pentru o operație $U$ pe $n$ qubiți, împreună cu o stare cuantică $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ pe $n$ qubiți \\\n"
"Promisiune: $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ este un vector propriu al lui $U$ \\\n"
"Ieșire: o aproximare a numărului $\\theta\\in[0,1)$ care satisface $U\\vert\\psi\\rangle = e^{2\\pi i \\theta}\\vert\\psi\\rangle$\n"
"</Figure>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here are a few remarks about this problem statement:\n"
msgstr "Iată câteva observații despre acest enunț al problemei:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The phase estimation problem is different from other problems we've seen so far in the course in that the input includes a quantum state. Typically we focus on problems having classical inputs and outputs, but nothing prevents us from considering quantum state inputs like this. In terms of its practical relevance, the phase estimation problem is typically encountered as a *subproblem* inside of a larger computation, like we'll see in the context of integer factorization later in the lesson.\n"
msgstr "Problema estimării fazei este diferită de alte probleme văzute până acum în curs prin faptul că intrarea include o stare cuantică. De obicei ne concentrăm pe probleme cu intrări și ieșiri clasice, dar nimic nu ne împiedică să luăm în considerare intrări sub formă de stări cuantice ca aceasta. Din perspectiva relevanței practice, problema estimării fazei este întâlnită de obicei ca o *subproblemă* în cadrul unui calcul mai mare, cum vom vedea în contextul factorizării numerelor întregi mai târziu în lecție.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The statement of the phase estimation problem above isn't specific about what constitutes an approximation of $\\theta$, but we can formulate more precise problem statements depending on our needs and interests. In the context of integer factorization, we'll demand a very precise approximation to $\\theta$, but in other cases we might be satisfied with a very rough approximation. We'll discuss shortly how the precision we require affects the computational cost of a solution.\n"
msgstr "Enunțul problemei de estimare a fazei de mai sus nu specifică ce constituie o aproximare a lui $\\theta$, dar putem formula enunțuri mai precise ale problemei în funcție de nevoile și interesele noastre. În contextul factorizării numerelor întregi, vom cere o aproximare foarte precisă a lui $\\theta$, dar în alte cazuri s-ar putea să fim mulțumiți cu o aproximare foarte grosieră. Vom discuta în scurt timp cum precizia necesară afectează costul computațional al unei soluții.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Notice that as we go from $\\theta = 0$ toward $\\theta = 1$ in the phase estimation problem, we're going all the way around the unit circle, starting from $e^{2\\pi i \\cdot 0} = 1$ and moving counter-clockwise toward $e^{2\\pi i \\cdot 1} = 1$. That is, when we reach $\\theta = 1$ we're back where we started at $\\theta = 0$. So, as we consider the accuracy of approximations, choices of $\\theta$ near $1$ should be considered as being near $0$. For example, an approximation $\\theta = 0.999$ should be considered as being within $1/1000$ of $\\theta = 0$.\n"
msgstr "Observă că pe măsură ce trecem de la $\\theta = 0$ spre $\\theta = 1$ în problema estimării fazei, parcurgem întreg cercul unitate, pornind de la $e^{2\\pi i \\cdot 0} = 1$ și deplasându-ne în sens invers acelor de ceasornic spre $e^{2\\pi i \\cdot 1} = 1$. Adică, atunci când ajungem la $\\theta = 1$ ne aflăm din nou la punctul de plecare$,\\theta = 0$. Prin urmare, când evaluăm acuratețea aproximărilor, alegerile lui $\\theta$ apropiate de $1$ trebuie considerate ca fiind apropiate de $0$. De exemplu, o aproximare $\\theta = 0.999$ trebuie considerată ca fiind la o distanță de $1/1000$ față de $\\theta = 0$.\n"
